.TH SANCHALA-NOTES 1 "2024" "Sanchala OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sanchala-notes \- Apple Notes-level note-taking application
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sanchala-notes
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sanchala Notes provides beautiful note-taking with folders, tags, and markdown support.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B new \fI[title]\fR
Create a new note
.TP
.B edit \fIid\fR
Edit an existing note in your default editor
.TP
.B show \fIid\fR
Display note contents
.TP
.B list, ls
List all notes
.TP
.B delete, rm \fIid\fR
Delete a note
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-search \fIquery\fR
Search notes by title or content
.TP
.B \-\-file \fIpath\fR
Import content from file when creating note
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Create a new note:
.B sanchala-notes new "Meeting Notes"
.TP
Search notes:
.B sanchala-notes list -s "project"
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/sanchala/notes/notes.db
SQLite database storing notes
.SH AUTHOR
Sanchala OS Team
